From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 09:30:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: the symbols guard ignores commented-out bodies,
 and the CUDA/Metal seed gaps the check found are closed (WI-1700 FIX-1/FIX-2)

FABLE-53-LOW's check of c9646c212 (ACCEPT-WITH-FIXES) found two holes in the symbols class.

FIX-1: _definition_present scanned raw text, so `// void foo(int x) {` or a body inside `/* */`
still read as a definition - a maker who disables a kernel by commenting it out passed the guard.
One left-to-right alternation now blanks `//...$` and `/*...*/` before matching, keeping string
literals verbatim so `"http://x"` is text and `/* http://x */` is one block comment. `#if 0` is
deliberately out of scope (docstring). New test: commented-out body in both comment styles is RED,
a `//` inside a block comment does not swallow the closer, a `//` inside a string or trailing a
definition line does not hide the body.

FIX-2: 5 of the 7 seed gaps the check listed are seeded (32 -> 37 symbols, all CHECKED defined at
c9646c212 and at lane-210/offrig-union-2026-09-06):
  metal-tq3-4s-kernels               ggml-metal.metal   kernel_get_rows_tq3_4s
  cuda-tq3-4s-kernels                tq3-native.cu      ggml_cuda_native_tq3_dot_kernel
  cuda-tq3-4s-kernels                mmq.cuh            ggml_cuda_mmq_load_tiles_tq3_4s
  moe-cache-heat-protected-eviction  ggml-metal.metal   kernel_moe_cache_mv_block_dot, kernel_moe_cache_mv_generic
mmq.cuh and ggml-metal.metal stay OUT of protected_paths on those entries - shared upstream files,
guarded by symbol not by path. NOT seeded: kernel_mul_mv_tq3_1s_f32 / kernel_tq3_rotate_act /
kernel_tq3_unrotate_act (series 0115, a `laguna` lift authored `m <m@l>`, grandfather row 37af31769
with no reaudit note) - a different mechanism, and the check gates it on HQ confirming authorship.

test_arifi_sync.py: 43 -> 44, OK in 138.7 s. validate --ref lane-210/offrig-union-2026-09-06 with this
tree: symbols 37/37 defined (WI-1699 restored by the R17 union); the two remaining rows are the
pre-existing UNREGISTERED 6ef196cd1/697027562, which lane-210's manifest already covers via
also_commits (19422b18d) and this branch's manifest predates.

